{"kind":"assert","text":"A sixth changed path, and I am asking rather than deciding.\n\nTHE FACT. At head 128132f23c3ea13e7b0ed93e33735f6181531c92 the diff against main touches seven files across six directories: cmd/gitseq-mcp, internal/residentclient, three documentation pages — and cmd/gs/main.go, four lines at resolveServerURL. Your conditions name five paths, \"the same exact paths the retired 4990f83b set covered\". cmd/gs is not among them, and it was not in that set either, though the earlier head changed the same four lines.\n\nWHAT THE CHANGE IS. Two error constructions move from literal format strings in cmd/gs to residentclient.UntrustedAdvertisement and residentclient.UnusableAdvertisedURL, the shared clauses this head adds. The user-visible sentences are preserved verbatim, which is why the commit message says cmd/gs is unchanged in behaviour. That is true of what it does and not true of what it contains.\n\nWHY I AM NOT JUST PUBLISHING A SIXTH ARTIFACT. Adding a path changes what the eventual merge retires there — cmd/gs currently carries one live artifact, 4ab0884a at 02558e8d — and that is a consequence of my publication, not of my implementation. Your conditions enumerate five paths for a stated reason, re-establishing coverage my own bare retirement removed, and cmd/gs was never in that hole. Widening the set on my own reading of what codex would want is the exact move that cost this lane three rounds already.\n\nWHAT I AM DOING MEANWHILE. Publishing the five you named, then requesting review, and telling codex plainly in the review request that cmd/gs changes at this head with no artifact standing at that path and why. That way the lane keeps moving and nobody discovers the gap by tripping over it.\n\nWHAT I NEED FROM YOU. Either widen this request to six paths, or say five is right and the cmd/gs edit is covered adequately by the residentclient artifact it delegates to. Both are defensible; the choice is yours, not mine. If codex requests a change on this point before you rule, I will treat that as the answer and come back to you with it."}